fun main() { var x = 1; print x; { x = 2; print x; } print x; }
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// w05_same_id.mini - my own example: the value changes, the ID does not.
//
// Prediction: every x here is the one declaration (ID 0). The block has no var,
// so x = 2 and the inner print find main's x. The last print sees 2, because
// the block changed the same variable.
//
// Try:  minic run w05/w05_same_id.mini   -> 1
//                                           2
//                                           2
//       minic cpp w05/w05_same_id.mini   -> every read and write uses mini_variable_0
//
// Compare week 04's w04_shadow_assign.mini: there the block has its own var x,
// so the assignment changed only the inner x and the outer one stayed 1.
